WEBVTT

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:36.580
The qualifiers for the world
championships have begun again this year.

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:39.000
And Zeo's been making his
way through the ranks.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.850
That's it! Go!

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.480
Don't lose, Zeronix!

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.610
Blow him back!

00:02:10.240 --> 00:02:16.320
But out of nowhere, Zeo
suddenly ran away from us.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:53.220
Why are you so obsessed with
the four Sacred Beasts' power?

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.110
Zeo, this is all for you!

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.760
For me?

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.890
What the heck is
that supposed to mean?

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:03.340
I have no idea what
you're going on about!

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:09.210
Zeo, you have an
important secret...

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.730
That I've not once
told you about.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.170
Master, are you su--

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.510
I don't care!

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.000
I knew this day
would come.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.470
Dad, what's this secret
you've never told me about?

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:39.560
Zeo, you're...

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.900
No, you're lying...

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:47.360
I can't believe that.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.210
You're lying!

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:58.940
This is what I
was fated to do.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.600
It's a fate I can't
escape from.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:05.120
So I will get the
four Sacred Beasts!

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:08.800
With Cerberus, I'll
do it without fail.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.620
Are the two
of you ready?

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.810
Yeah!

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.620
Gordo, don't hold back.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:20.190
Attack like you intend
to destroy Cerberus.

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:22.820
Yes, Doctor Zagart.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:24.040
Let's do it, Zeo!

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.170
Bring it!

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:33.000
Cerberus!

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.320
Go!!

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:44.790
What amazing power.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:48.000
Go, go, go!
Push him out!

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:53.620
You must withstand it, Zeo.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:55.450
All of this
is for you.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.890
I won't lose!

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:04.000
Here it comes.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:07.300
Gordo, keep attacking!

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.250
Go!!

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:13.960
Darn!

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:20.290
Excellent. Cerberus's Sacred
Beast index is beginning to rise.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:22.310
Go!

00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:32.020
I will not lose.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:36.400
I will... I will obtain
all four Sacred Beasts!

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:45.470
Cerberus!

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:51.780
There it is!

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.670
No! The Sacred Beast
can't materialize!

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:11.270
The Beyblade is being
overwhelmed by the Sacred Beast!

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:15.560
Is this the power of Cerberus, the
strongest of all Sacred Beasts from the tablet?

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.690
Zeo, you must withstand it.

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.410
I will not lose...

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:25.130
I refuse to lose!

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:40.500
One more time, Zeo.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:55.810
--Go, Shoot!

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.200
Go!

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.700
I won't lose!

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.050
Cerberus!

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.600
This time...

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:53.970
Go, Shoot!

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:04.710
Cerberus!!

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:14.890
Don't lose!

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.260
He did it!

00:08:36.440 --> 00:08:38.100
Go, Driger!

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.870
Keep it up, Rei.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.580
Leave me alone!

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:51.040
What's wrong, Zeo?

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:52.930
Leave me alone!

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:56.490
Stay away! We're through!

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:57.500
Stay away!

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.100
From here on out, we're enemies.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.330
Forget everything
we've been through!

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:04.120
How could we forget?

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.620
What's gotten into you?

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:07.700
Kinomiya.

00:09:08.510 --> 00:09:11.230
Next time we meet,
I will defeat you!

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:15.470
Wait, Zeo!

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:16.530
Zeo!

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:21.950
Zeo...

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:23.520
What are you...

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.400
What happened?

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:31.410
Zeo!

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:37.860
Hiromi!

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:42.560
Made it!

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:46.880
There we go!

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:48.180
What's this junk?

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:49.540
Fortune telling books!

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:50.860
Fortune telling?

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.840
Horoscopes...
Blood types...

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:55.200
Flower fortunes...

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.720
Zoological fortunes?

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.960
There's even a
book for tarot cards!

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.110
Are these all yours, Hiromi?

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:03.710
Yup! I've got even
more at home.

00:10:03.710 --> 00:10:05.910
Wow, I had no idea!

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.390
Who'd have thought
you'd be into this?

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:10.360
Fortune telling is
love's secret weapon!

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:13.240
And I'm a maiden
who dreams of love!

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:16.800
Maybe you should look
in a mirror once in a while.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:18.120
Did you say something?

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.610
Nope, nothing!

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:22.090
So what brings
up fortune telling?

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:23.380
To decide pairings!

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:24.240
For the tournament?

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:27.180
The block qualifiers
are about to end.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:30.600
So the four of you need to decide
on pairings and get to practicing.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:35.320
This way we'd be able to
practice a little more realistically.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:37.620
So why do we need
fortune telling for that?

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:42.530
You just don't get it. Teamwork is the most important part of a tag match!

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:45.940
We'll use fortune telling
to make the perfect pairs!

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:48.630
I get it, so that's where
the fortune telling comes in.

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:51.100
What a load of crap.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:55.730
I've been looking through them since
yesterday but couldn't make a decision.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:11:01.370
According to zoological fortune telling, Takao and Max, and Rei and Kai are good pairs.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:05.210
But according to
these horoscopes...

00:11:05.210 --> 00:11:07.090
They're the
worst matchups.

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:08.310
Right?

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:12.080
But your luck will be higher
during the tournament Max,

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:15.210
So I think you can
cover for Takao, too!

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:17.330
There's a lot to this...

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:19.940
Hiromi, how is this?

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:23.850
This says that Takao and
Rei would be a good pair...

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:25.500
Let me see.

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:30.020
This won't do. During the
tournament, Mars will align with Virgo.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:33.050
So it's backwards!

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:36.660
You're right.
This would be bad.

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:38.890
Oh come on, guys!

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:42.480
Are you really going to decide pairs with some dumb fortune telling?

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.360
It's not dumb!

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:46.220
Fortune telling is...

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:49.420
It's just some
dumb girly hobby!

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:50.610
Don't go there!

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:53.090
Battles happen
in the stadium!

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:56.240
Who cares where Mars is?

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:58.540
This fortune telling
stuff is just...

00:11:58.540 --> 00:11:59.900
Takao...

00:12:00.680 --> 00:12:03.090
Don't make fun
of fortune telling!

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:15.100
Why do I have to put
up with this crap?

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:18.810
Because the way you run your mouth tends to start fights.

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:23.280
Hiromi's taking this seriously.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:24.200
Yeah!

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.920
Why am I always
the bad guy?

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:29.580
Why are you guys
so soft on Hiromi?

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.300
Done!

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:35.120
So the pairs will be Takao and Max, and then Kai and myself.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:41.640
I input the attack and defense of your Beys, along with your personalities and patterns.

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:43.880
And these are
the results.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:49.280
With these, even against
attack types or defense types,

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:52.740
you'll be able to bring out the most
of your strengths in any situation.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:55.620
So that's it
for the pairs.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:56.980
Are you okay
with this, Takao?

00:12:56.980 --> 00:12:58.400
Yeah.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:02.200
Look, turns out the zoological
fortune telling was right after all.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:05.140
Fortunes know all!

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.980
Listen, you!

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:09.180
Calm down...

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:19.440
"Bakuten Shoot Beyblade 2002"

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:30.090
The qualifiers for the A block
are about to wrap up!

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:34.460
And their battle is
getting heated up!

00:13:35.060 --> 00:13:36.740
Look at 'em go!

00:13:36.740 --> 00:13:38.660
They're all pretty good!

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:42.130
Just watching is getting
me ready to battle!

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:46.120
Now that the pairs have been set,
I can't wait to get in there!

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:47.800
Kyoujyu!

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:49.600
Hiromi!

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:51.920
Over here!

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:56.270
Toru's going in!
Is this the match?

00:13:57.130 --> 00:13:59.860
Neither of them
have decent Beys.

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:03.800
Some world championships these are.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:06.980
--Let's go.

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:08.580
This is a huge upset!
The battle isn't over yet!

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:32.480
You're not half bad.

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:36.700
Way better than some kids happy
to play in some silly tournament.

00:14:39.820 --> 00:14:42.960
Either way, that Attack Ring
is such a waste on you.

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:47.420
If we used it, our attack power
would double. No, triple.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:50.020
Who are you two?

00:14:50.020 --> 00:14:52.700
No one special.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.380
Well? Would you
like to battle me?

00:14:58.210 --> 00:15:01.670
If you win, you can take
whatever parts you like.

00:15:02.240 --> 00:15:06.720
But if I win, I'll take that
Attack Ring off your hands.

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:08.460
What do you say?

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.380
No thanks.

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:13.760
I don't have time
to battle you.

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:15.090
What?

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:28.050
Are you in the
mood to battle now?

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:35.680
Let's do it.

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:38.880
Three! Two! One!

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:40.710
Go, Shoot!

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:45.220
Go, Uriel!

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:46.720
Dranzer!

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.440
You're better
than I thought.

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:54.420
King, don't hold back.
Wrap this up quickly!

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:56.010
Leave it to me.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.940
Uriel!

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:03.100
He's strong. These
guys aren't all talk.

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:06.360
That's it, King.
Keep up the pressure!

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:07.780
Go!

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.780
I won't lose!

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:13.960
What?!

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:16.380
He blew him back!

00:16:16.380 --> 00:16:18.920
I'm getting more and more
interested in that Attack Ring.

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:19.820
King!

00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:21.060
Yeah!

00:16:21.060 --> 00:16:23.400
Uriel!!

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:33.180
What?! You have
a Sacred Beast?

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:36.980
What does it matter?
Your Attack Ring is mine.

00:16:36.980 --> 00:16:38.130
Go!

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:45.380
Suzaku!

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:52.200
A Sacred Beast?!

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:58.660
I get it. You've got a
Sacred Beast of your own!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.840
Now this is getting fun!

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:04.940
Go, Uriel!!

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:08.000
Dranzer!!

00:17:15.890 --> 00:17:18.940
He's evenly
matched with Uriel!

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:21.440
Dranzer!!

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:26.660
Uriel!

00:17:27.420 --> 00:17:28.800
You're finished!

00:17:28.800 --> 00:17:30.200
No he's not!

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.880
Gabriel!!

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:44.100
We're just
getting started!

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:46.920
Show me what
you've got!

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:49.130
Uriel!!

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:54.920
Suzaku!

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:56.440
--Go!

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:03.720
What's wrong?
Where'd all your fight go?

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.020
Go!

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:09.810
Darn...

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:12.140
Let's wrap this up.

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.530
King!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:14.960
<b>Okay, go!</b>

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:20.660
I'm not going down...
Dranzer!

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.560
--What?!

00:18:28.610 --> 00:18:30.880
--We underestimated you.
--King...

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:31.560
Yeah.

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:33.660
--Double Attack!

00:18:41.200 --> 00:18:42.490
Suzaku!

00:18:54.700 --> 00:18:56.320
We overdid it.

00:18:56.320 --> 00:18:59.400
I thought it was a pretty
good Attack Ring, too.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:01.530
But we went
and broke it.

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:02.740
Let's go.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:09.820
Dranzer...

00:19:09.820 --> 00:19:12.120
Dranzer's split in half!

00:19:12.970 --> 00:19:15.800
What happened, Kai?

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:23.980
So that's it?

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:25.330
Can you fix it?

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:31.850
The Bit Chip is fine, but with all this
damage, I'll have to make a new Beyblade.

00:19:32.140 --> 00:19:36.520
But they attacked him
two on one! That's low!

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.360
Who the heck were they?

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.720
Could it be King and
Queen, the parts hunters?

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:42.980
Parts hunters?

00:19:42.980 --> 00:19:45.170
I've heard of them.

00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:51.210
They ask for a match, and then take parts
from the loser! They don't play fair.

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:54.640
They're pretty
infamous Bladers.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:57.480
King and Queen,
the parts hunters...

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.770
I'll never forgive them!

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:03.900
How dare they
treat Beys like that!

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:07.180
Kai, I'll get
revenge for you!

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:10.170
I appreciate it,
but this is my problem.

00:20:10.170 --> 00:20:12.410
I'll get my
own revenge.

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:25.690
Show me the fruits
of your labor!

00:20:27.780 --> 00:20:29.980
Three! Two! One!

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:31.790
Go, Shoot!

00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:36.210
Cerberus!

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:49.530
I will not lose!

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:59.340
Go, Gordo!
Repel Cerberus!

00:20:59.340 --> 00:21:01.030
Go!!

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:03.030
Cerberus!

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:23.860
You've done it!
You've mastered Cerberus!

00:21:25.700 --> 00:21:29.620
I challenge you, Kinomiya.
I will defeat Dragoon.

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:33.620
And then I will obtain Seiryu and the
rest of the four Sacred Beasts!

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:03.050
The world championships
are starting to heat up.

00:23:03.050 --> 00:23:07.200
King and Queen
appear before us.

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:10.450
Kai wants his revenge,
but who wins?

00:23:10.450 --> 00:23:13.760
What? You like revenge
too, Chairman?

00:23:13.760 --> 00:23:16.690
It's very sweet,
sour, and fruity?

00:23:16.690 --> 00:23:19.240
That's an orange!
Not revenge!

00:23:19.240 --> 00:23:21.300
Watch the next episode, too!
